        <technology>
            <technologyDescriptionAndIncludedProcesses xml:lang="en">Production from sodium sulfide nonahydrate (itself produced out of sodium hydroxide and hydrogen sulfide) and P-dichlorobenzene in an N-methyl-2-pyrrolidone solution with a yield of 85%. Inventory bases on patent information. The emissions to air (0.2 wt.% of raw material input) and water were estimated using mass balance. Treatment of the waste water in a internal waste water treatment plant assumed (elimination efficiency of 90% for C).\n\n# Included processes\nRaw materials and chemicals used for production, transport of materials to manufacturing plant, estimated emissions to air and water from production (incomplete), estimation of energy demand and infrastructure of the plant (approximation). Solid wastes omitted.</technologyDescriptionAndIncludedProcesses>
        </technology>
    </processInformation>
